WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Prism opens Broken Circuitry: Reassembly, 17 tracks at 97.5 BPM. Clicking the glass track at bar 19 opens its notes in the piano roll.

00:05.000 --> 00:12.000
Select the C7, drag its velocity to 90%, then drag the track's Space reverb send down. Each edit is saved to the project file.

00:12.000 --> 00:22.000
The Patch page shows glass's voice: additive partials through a smoother. Drag a Delay in from the module list.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000
Click an output socket, then an input socket, to wire the smoother into the delay and the delay into the output.

00:28.000 --> 00:33.000
The inspector lists each module's parameters and connections. Play auditions the patch.

00:33.000 --> 00:39.000
Mix shows every track's gain, pan, output bus and Space send. Pulling glow's send down shows its group bus: EQ and a compressor keyed from the kick.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.000
Space is the shared reverb: size, decay and damping.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
Back on the Timeline, Play renders bars 19 and 20 from the edited project. The render wait is cut.

00:47.000 --> 00:59.000
What you hear is the audio Osprey rendered, edits included.
